# The annotations of the resident $F000-$FFFF (tape blocks 25, 17 and 27 of the SpeedLock group, XOR $DF, moved
# into place by Boot): the source of src/resident/resident.asm (../../kit/mkgame.py --part src/resident/resident.json).
# Format: ../../../../docs/ann-format.md. Witnesses: c1 (work/stage1/c1, the load, the menu and stage 1) and the
# recordings of WALKTHROUGH 6 (menu, deaths, s1-idle, sN-right). The L1 windows start at $F03F: every stage block
# loads $6C3F-$F03E, over ResidentInit, so the counts below $F03F would be the stages' own. c1's witness counts are
# its window from the resident's entry on (work/stage1/c1/run, frames 5166-16658, tools/c1_windows.sh): the chain and
# the loader ran at the same addresses before it, and one L1 keeps one instruction an address.

@equ $4000 Screen 6144 ; the bitmap
@equ $5800 Attributes 768 ; the attributes
@isub $F003 LD SP,$FFFF
@isub $F5D9 LD HL,50000
@equ $5B00 TextBuffer 256 ; TextToBuffer's line of text, 32 bytes a pixel row, 8 rows
@equ $5D00 GlyphBuffer 14 ; one glyph shifted into place, 2 bytes a row
@equ $6C3F GameBlock ; where every turbo block loads: the front ($6C3F-$A83E) or a stage ($6C3F-$F03E)
@equ $7800 GameMain ; the front's FrontMain and each stage's entry (src/front, src/stageN)
@equ $BB80 StageCheckByte ; the byte of a loaded stage block that names it (StageCheck)

@module init ; Start-up: silence, the IM 2 set-up, the front
@about Boot jumps to ResidentEntry. ResidentInit silences the AY, saves the turbo loader's bytes under the IM 2 jump, sets IM 2 with Im2Handler, marks no stage loaded and loads the front, then runs it. The front returns into NewGame when START GAME is chosen.

$F000 c ResidentInit ; Border black, SP = $FFFF, silence, IM 2 on Im2Handler, no stage loaded, then the front
> Run once, from ResidentEntry (c1: the front loads after it; the stage blocks overwrite $F000-$F03E later, so ResidentInit is gone once a stage is loaded and the restart path goes to RestartFromStageOne instead). StageLoaded := $FF (none).
$F017 ; to ShowFront

$F019 b ResidentInitPad ; Zeros up to ResidentEntry, overwritten by every stage block
> No code reads them: the stage blocks load $6C3F-$F03E over them (their last bytes, the stages' own). Known only from the code and tape.txt.

$F040 c ResidentEntry ; Interrupts off, then ResidentInit
> Boot's JP (HL) lands here (c1). Witness: L1 1 (c1).

$F043 c ShowFront ; Clear the screen and load the front
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).

$F048 c RestartFromStageOne ; REWIND THE TAPE, AND THEN PRESS PLAY, wait, then load the front again
> GameOver's second option (RESTART FROM STAGE ONE) jumps here: the front is the tape's first turbo block, so the tape has to go back. Not executed in any recording (the recordings checked: no game over chose it); known only from the code ($F2EE).
$F04B ; Print: the text follows

$F04E t TextRewind ; The text: column byte 9, bit 3, row 36, REWIND THE TAPE
@res resident/text-rewind.bin

$F061 c RestartFromStageOne2 ; Print the second line
$F064 t TextPressPlayAgain ; The text: column byte 7, bit 5, row 52, AND THEN PRESS PLAY
@res resident/text-press-play-again.bin

$F07B c RestartFromStageOne3 ; WaitFrames, then into LoadFront

$F07E c LoadFront ; Load the front (stage 0: B 3, H 2, L 1, 30 pages of 512 bytes) and run it
> LoadStage with C = 0: StageLoaded := 0, so LoadBlock does not check the block. Then CALL GameMain: the front; START GAME returns to NewGame below. Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$F08D ; the front; START GAME comes back here

@module game ; The game: the stage chain, PlayStage, the game over menu
@about NewGame starts a game with 5 lives and 4 credits, then plays the five stages in order: a stage completed (E = 2 from the stage's code) goes on to the next; a lost one goes to GameOver, which retries it (RESTART THIS STAGE, a credit less) or jumps to RestartFromStageOne. Stage 5 loops on itself.

$F090 c NewGame ; Score and amount 0, lives 5, credits 4, then the five stages in turn
> Reached from the front's StartGame by RET (front notes). Witness: L1 4 (c1, joystick, menu, rzx-r0).
$F0A4 PlayStage1 ; stage 1 until completed
$F0B2 PlayStage2
$F0C0 PlayStage3
$F0CE PlayStage4
$F0DC PlayStage5 ; stage 5: the same either way

$F0EA b StageTable ; The five stages: the load parameters, then the two title lines as Print data
> A record: D, E (not read by the resident: LoadStage keeps B, H, L; known only from the code), C the stage number (StageLoaded, StageCheck), H, L and B (the length: 2 x (9B + H + L) pages of 256 bytes, 132 = 33 792 bytes for every stage), then two Print strings (column byte, bit, row, text, 0): STAGE N and its title. Read by PlayStage (c1: stage 1; sN-right: stages 2-5).
@res resident/stages.bin
$F111 StageRecord2
$F13E StageRecord3
$F172 StageRecord4
$F1A1 StageRecord5

$F1CA c PlayStage ; Show the titles, load the stage at IY (unless loaded), run it; Z when it was completed
> Input: IY a StageTable record. ClearScreen; if StageLoaded is not the record's stage, PRESS PLAY ON TAPE, WaitFrames, and the line cleared again. The two titles with PrintRecord. Then StageLoadLoop: LoadStage until it gives Z (the right block, StageCheck), each failure marking no stage loaded. SilenceAy, ClearScreen, H := Lives, CALL GameMain (the stage), Lives := H, CP E with 2, SilenceAy. Output: Z when the stage ended with E = 2 (completed), BC the address of the stage's score digits for GameOver. Witness: L1 8 (c1, joystick, menu, rzx-r0-rzx-r4).
$F1DC ; Print: the text follows
$F1DF t TextPressPlay ; The text: column byte 8, bit 2, row 52, PRESS PLAY ON TAPE
@res resident/text-press-play.bin
$F1F5 c PlayStage2nd ; wait, then clear the line
$F1FB t TextClearLine ; The text: column byte 8, bit 2, row 52, a space (clears the line: TextToBuffer clears the buffer)
@res resident/text-clear-line.bin
$F200 c PlayStageTitles ; the record's two title lines
$F211 StageLoadLoop ; load until the block is the stage's
$F22F StageRun ; the stage itself

$F24B c GameOver ; GAME OVER: a credit less, the menu RESTART THIS STAGE / RESTART FROM STAGE ONE, SPACE chooses
> Input: BC the address of the stage's six score digits (copied into the menu's SCORE). Credits := Credits - 1 (the POKE "credits 62045,0" is the DEC A at $F25D, src/tape notes), shown as a digit. ClearScreen, GAME OVER, PRESS SPACE TO SELECT, 20 rounds of HALT + CycleColours (which HALTs again): 40 frames, the menu. Every 64 frames (32 rounds of two HALTs, FrameCounter AND $1F = 0) the highlight moves to the other line (with no credit left it stays on RESTART FROM STAGE ONE); SPACE takes the highlighted one: RESTART THIS STAGE sets Lives := 5 and returns (PlayStage again), RESTART FROM STAGE ONE drops the return and jumps to RestartFromStageOne. Witness: L1 4 (s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right).
$F25D CreditsDec ; DEC A: the credit a game over costs
$F269 ; Print: the text follows
$F26C t TextGameOver ; The text: column byte 12, bit 0, row 40, GAME OVER
@res resident/text-game-over.bin
$F279 c GameOver2 ; Print the second line
$F27C t TextPressSpace ; The text: column byte 7, bit 0, row 52, PRESS SPACE TO SELECT
@res resident/text-press-space.bin
$F295 c GameOver3 ; 40 frames of colours (20 rounds of two HALTs), the menu, then the choice
$F297 GameOverPause
$F2A7 GameOverLoop ; one frame; GameOver4's CycleColours HALTs again, so a round is two frames
$F2BA GameOverToggle
$F2C3 GameOverSetOption
$F2D0 ; AttrBox: the highlight bar, its row patched above

$F2D3 b HighlightBox 5 ; AttrBox data: column 0, row (10 + 2 x option, written at $F2CA), 32 wide, 1 high, attribute $43
$F2D4 HighlightRow ; the row, written by GameOver

$F2D8 c GameOver4 ; CycleColours, then SPACE (port $7FFE bit 0)
$F2F1 GameOverRetry ; RESTART THIS STAGE: Lives := 5, return

$F2F7 c PrintGameOverMenu ; Print the two options and the credits and score line
> Witness: L1 4 (s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right).
$F2FA t TextRestartStage ; The text: column byte 8, bit 5, row 84, RESTART THIS STAGE
@res resident/text-restart-stage.bin
$F310 c PrintGameOverMenu2
$F313 t TextRestartFromOne ; The text: column byte 6, bit 3, row 100, RESTART FROM STAGE ONE
@res resident/text-restart-from-one.bin
$F32D c PrintGameOverMenu3
$F330 t TextCreditsScore ; The text: column byte 1, bit 6, row 148, GAME CREDITS n   SCORE nnnnnn (n written by GameOver)
@res resident/text-credits-score.bin
$F340 CreditsDigit ; the credits digit, written by GameOver
$F34E ScoreDigits ; the six score digits, copied by GameOver
$F355 c PrintGameOverMenuEnd

@module print ; Text and screen: the proportional print, the reveal, the attribute boxes, the colour cycle, the screen clear, the dissolve masks
@about Print takes its text after the CALL: a column byte, a bit within it, a pixel row, then capital letters, digits and spaces up to a 0. TextToBuffer draws the line into TextBuffer with PrintFont (each glyph its own width), then RevealText brings it onto the screen in 8 frames through the dissolve masks, while CycleColours runs. AttrBox fills an attribute rectangle given after its CALL. ClearScreen clears the screen and paints the colour bands of the title screens.

$F356 c CycleColours ; One HALT, then FrameCounter + 1, the next colour of ColourCycle into the box under the titles
> Called once a round by the waits (c1, every recording with a title screen); every resident caller HALTs before it, so in the resident's loops FrameCounter steps once every two frames. Witness: L1 7883 (c1, ending, joystick, menu, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r5).
$F36B ; AttrBox: the cycling box

$F36E b CycleBox 5 ; AttrBox data: column 6, row 4, 20 wide, 4 high, the attribute written by CycleColours
$F372 CycleBoxAttr ; the attribute

$F373 c CycleColoursEnd ; RET

$F374 b ColourCycle 8 ; The box's colours, one a frame: bright red, magenta, green, cyan, yellow and back
> Read by CycleColours (c1).
@res resident/colour-cycle.bin

$F37C c AttrBox ; Fill an attribute box: column, row, width, height, attribute after the CALL
> The five bytes after the CALL: column, row, width, height, attribute; returns after them. Witness: L1 9085 (c1, ending, joystick, menu, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r5).
$F394 AttrBoxRow
$F39C AttrBoxCell

$F3B0 c Print ; Print the text after the CALL: TextToBuffer, then RevealText at its row
> The data: column byte, bit, pixel row, text, 0; returns after the 0. Witness: L1 43 (c1, joystick, menu, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r4).

$F3BD c PrintRecord ; Print the text at IY (a StageTable title), IY past it
> Witness: L1 11 (c1, joystick, menu, rzx-r0, rzx-r1, rzx-r3).

$F3CB c TextToBuffer ; Draw the text at IY (column byte, bit, row, text, 0) into TextBuffer with PrintFont
> Clears TextBuffer, sets BitShift and TextRow; for each character: A-Z, a space (as the glyph after Z) and 0-9 (after the space); the glyph's width mask to CharMask, its 7 rows to GlyphBuffer, shifted right by BitShift, ORed into TextBuffer at DE; then Advance. Ends after the 0 with IY past it. Witness: L1 54 (c1, joystick, menu, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r4).
$F3F3 TextNextChar
$F409 TextNotDigit
$F40F TextGlyph
$F428 TextGlyphRow
$F43B TextShift
$F440 TextShiftRow
$F44B TextMerge
$F450 TextMergeRow
$F482 TextEnd

$F465 c Advance ; Move BitShift and DE on by the glyph's width: 9 less the trailing zeros of CharMask
> Witness: L1 760 (c1, joystick, menu, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r4).
$F46A AdvanceCount
$F473 AdvanceAdd
$F47E AdvanceStore

$F483 c RevealText ; Bring TextBuffer onto the screen from pixel row A in 8 frames through the dissolve masks
> For step 0-7: the ADD A,n at RevealMaskAdd := $CB + step; HALT, CycleColours; for the 7 rows and 32 bytes: mask = DissolveMasks set (a ROM byte from $0001 up AND $18) at the step; screen := (screen AND NOT mask) OR (buffer AND mask). Witness: L1 54 (c1, joystick, menu, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r4).
$F490 RevealStep
$F4AD RevealRow
$F4BA RevealByte
$F4C7 RevealMaskAdd ; ADD A,n: n = $CB + step, written above

$F4E5 c WaitBC ; Wait BC frames (HALT each)
> Witness: L1 0 ().

$F4EC c ClearScreen ; Black attributes, a clear bitmap, then the colour bands of rows 18-22 and SetMenuBands
> Witness: L1 28 (c1, ending, joystick, menu, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r5).
$F4EF b ClearBox 5 ; AttrBox data: the whole screen, attribute 0
$F4F4 c ClearScreen2 ; the bitmap
$F504 b BandRow18 5 ; AttrBox data: row 18, attribute $42
$F509 c ClearScreen3
$F50C b BandRow19 5 ; AttrBox data: row 19, attribute $03
$F511 c ClearScreen4
$F514 b BandRow21 5 ; AttrBox data: row 21, attribute $42
$F519 c ClearScreen5
$F51C b BandRow22 5 ; AttrBox data: row 22, attribute $03

$F521 c SetMenuBands ; The colour bands of rows 10-15 (the titles' rows)
> Also called by GameOver for each highlight move. Witness: L1 217 (c1, ending, joystick, menu, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r5).
$F524 b BandRows10 5 ; AttrBox data: rows 10-17, attribute $44
$F529 c SetMenuBands2
$F52C b BandRow11 5 ; AttrBox data: row 11, attribute $05
$F531 c SetMenuBands3
$F534 b BandRow13 5 ; AttrBox data: row 13, attribute $05
$F539 c SetMenuBands4
$F53C b BandRow15 5 ; AttrBox data: row 15, attribute $05
$F541 c SetMenuBandsEnd

$F542 c WaitFrames ; 75 rounds of HALT + CycleColours (two HALTs): 150 frames, 3 s
> Witness: L1 15 (c1, ending, joystick, menu, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r0-rzx-r5).
$F544 WaitFramesLoop

@module ay ; The AY driver: the effects and the three channels
@about A stage plays an effect with CALL PlaySoundVector, E the effect number. StartEffect puts the effect into its channel (1-3); Im2Handler runs AyFrame every frame, which steps each busy channel: a segment's period and volume change each frame for its duration, then the next segment, and the channel goes quiet after the last. Every AY write is an OUT to $FFFD (the register) and $BFFD (the value): on a 48K these do nothing.

$F54D b EffectData ; The 13 effects: channel, noise flag (0 a tone), segments, volume x 16, period, then the segments
> With the noise flag set the channel's tone is off, its noise on, and AyFrame writes the period's low byte to the noise period (register 6). A segment: duration in frames, period change a frame (signed), volume change a frame (signed, x 16). Read by StartEffect and ChannelStep (every stage recording).
@res resident/effects.bin
$F556 Effect1
$F55F Effect2
$F568 Effect3
$F571 Effect4
$F57A Effect5
$F58F Effect6
$F59B Effect7
$F5A4 Effect8
$F5AD Effect9
$F5B9 Effect10
$F5C5 Effect11
$F5CE Effect12

$F5D7 b EffectLeftover 2 ; Two bytes after the last effect that no code reads: $06 $04, like the start of a second segment
> Effect 12 has one segment, so ChannelStep stops before them (known only from the code: the count at $F5D0 is 1). A leftover of the effect's editing.

@module game ; The game

$F5D9 c DelayB ; B times 50 000 loop passes
> Not executed in any recording (all checked); stage 4's code refers to it (known only from the code: work/stage2/loader/xref.txt).
$F5DC DelayBLoop

@module stageload ; The stage loader
@about LoadStage loads the turbo block of the stage C (LoadBlock and TurboLoad), unless it is already in memory. Every turbo block has the flag $56 and the stage blocks have one length, so the loader takes whichever stage block comes next on the tape; LoadBlock then compares the block's byte at StageCheckByte with StageCheck for the stage wanted. A wrong block gives NZ: PlayStage marks no stage loaded and loads again, with no message. So a tape wound on to another stage loads that stage's block, rejects it and waits for the next block; only the stage wanted is accepted, and the stage wanted moves on only when a stage is completed.

$F5E4 c LoadStage ; Load stage C's block (B, H, L its length) unless it is the one loaded; Z when it is in memory
> Inputs: C the stage (0 the front), B, H, L the length parameters (to LoadLength). StageLoaded = C: wait 120 frames, Z. Else StageLoaded := C, HALT, LoadBlock; NZ (a wrong block or a load error) returns NZ; else clear the line, STOP THE TAPE, WaitFrames, Z. Witness: L1 7 (c1, joystick, menu, stageload, rzx-r0, rzx-r1).
$F5FF ; Print: the text follows
$F602 t TextClearTop ; The text: column 0, bit 0, row 36, a space
@res resident/text-clear-top.bin
$F607 c LoadStage2
$F60A t TextStopTape ; The text: column byte 10, bit 3, row 52, STOP THE TAPE
@res resident/text-stop-tape.bin
$F61B c LoadStage3 ; WaitFrames, then Z
$F623 LoadStageLoaded ; already in memory: 120 frames, Z

@module im2 ; The IM 2 set-up, the handler and the table

$F629 c SaveLoaderBytes ; Copy the three bytes at Im2Jump (TurboLoad's code) to SavedLoaderBytes
> Witness: L1 5 (c1, joystick, stageload).

$F635 c SetIm2 ; Im2Jump := JP HL, I := $FD, IM 2, EI
> Im2Table ($FD00-$FE00, all $FE) sends every interrupt to Im2Jump at $FEFE. Witness: L1 5 (c1, joystick, stageload).

@module print ; Text and screen

$F646 c CopyToScreen ; Copy B rows of D bytes from HL to the screen at row C, column A (via ScreenLineTable)
> Not executed in any recording (all checked), no reference from the front or a stage (xref.txt). Known only from the code ($F646-$F66B).
$F656 CopyToScreenRow
$F65A CopyColumnAdd ; ADD A,n: n the column, written above

@module im2 ; The IM 2 set-up, the handler and the table

$F66C b SavedLoaderBytes 3 ; TurboLoad's three bytes at Im2Jump while the IM 2 jump is there
> Written by SaveLoaderBytes, read back by LoadBlock (c1).

