@module keys ; The key readers
@about Five readers, one per control. Each calls KeyHook (a RET), reads its port, XORs KeyXorMask and tests its bit: Z when the control is on (keys are active low). The front's DEFINE KEYS and SELECT JOYSTICK rewrite the port word at +4 and the BIT byte at +13 of each. The tape's defaults: I J Q W O (front notes).

$FC90 c KeyUp ; UP: port $DFFE bit 2 (I)
> Witness: L1 41801 (c1, c1o, deaths, ending, joystick, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r1-rzx-r5).
$FC9F c KeyDown ; DOWN: port $BFFE bit 3 (J)
> Witness: L1 33044 (c1, c1o, deaths, ending, joystick, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r1-rzx-r5).
$FCAE c KeyLeft ; LEFT: port $FBFE bit 0 (Q)
> Witness: L1 37050 (c1, c1o, deaths, ending, joystick, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r1-rzx-r5).
$FCBD c KeyRight ; RIGHT: port $FBFE bit 1 (W)
> Witness: L1 40953 (c1, c1o, deaths, ending, joystick, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r1-rzx-r5).
$FCCC c KeyFire ; FIRE: port $DFFE bit 1 (O)
> Witness: L1 49911 (c1, c1o, deaths, ending, joystick, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r1-rzx-r5).

$FCDB c KeyHook ; RET: each reader calls it first
> Witness: L1 787888 (c1, c1o, deaths, ending, joystick, s1-idle, s1-right, s2-right, s3-right, s4-right, s5-right, stageload, rzx-r1-rzx-r5).

$FCDC c KeyHookExit ; Not executed in any recording: on a key bit 0 clear, IM 0, the stack and return the front saved, Im2Jump back from SavedIm2Jump
> All recordings checked. KeyHook's RET at $FCDB keeps it out of reach; with the RET replaced by a NOP the readers would run it. Known only from the code ($FCDC-$FCF9).

$FCFA b KeyXorMask ; 0 for keys (active low), $FF for a Kempston (active high), written by the front
$FCFB b KeyXorMaskPad 5 ; Zeros no code reads (known only from the code)

@module im2 ; The IM 2 set-up, the handler and the table

$FD00 b Im2Table 16 ; 257 bytes of $FE: whatever the bus holds, the vector is $FEFE (Im2Jump)
> Read by the Z80 at every interrupt (I = $FD), c1 and every recording.

@module vars ; The resident's variables and the stages' work space

$FE01 b WorkSpace 16 ; The work space of the front and the stages (zeros in the tape's image)
> The front: SavedIm2Jump, SavedStack, SavedReturn, ShimmerCount, ReaderBitOp, ReaderPort (src/front). The stages: $FE08-$FE6F (src/stageN). The resident's own: GameOverOption and FrameCounter.
$FE04 SavedStack
$FE06 SavedReturn
$FE08 StageVars
$FE1D ShimmerCount
$FE1E GameOverOption ; GameOver's highlighted line, 0 or 1
$FE1F StageVars2
$FE31 FrameCounter ; CycleColours' frame count
$FE32 StageVars3
$FE4C ReaderBitOp
$FE4D ReaderPort
$FE4F StageVars4

@module turbo ; The turbo loader
@about TurboLoad reads one block of the game: flag $56, then D x 256 bytes to GameBlock, the ROM's LD-BYTES method with its own timing. Its three bytes at $FEFE-$FF00 are also Im2Jump: LoadBlock puts them back before it loads and SetIm2 writes the JP again after.

$FE90 c TurboLoad ; Load a block of 2 x (9B + H + L) pages (LoadLength) to GameBlock; carry set when it loaded
> Witness: L1 7 (c1, joystick, menu, stageload, rzx-r0, rzx-r1).
$FEB1 TurboExit ; border black; carry set: return; else RST 8 report R (Tape loading error)
$FEB9 TurboStart ; flag $56, the pilot, the sync, the bytes
$FED1 TurboPilot
$FED3 TurboPilotEdge
$FEE2 TurboSync
$FEFD TurboByte ; the flag byte first, then the data
$FEFE Im2Jump ; JR NZ: also where SetIm2 writes JP Im2Handler
$FF07 TurboFlag ; the first byte must be $56
$FF11 TurboVerify ; the verify path: never taken (the flag's carry says LOAD)
$FF16 TurboNext
$FF18 TurboCount
$FF1C TurboBits
$FF1E TurboBit

$FF37 c TurboEdgePair ; Two edges
> Witness: L1 936052 (c1, joystick, menu, stageload).
$FF3B TurboEdge ; one edge: count B up while EAR stays; the border from it
$FF3C TurboEdgeLoop
$FF4C TurboBorderMask ; AND n: 2 at the pilot, 1 for the data

@module stageload ; The stage loader

$FF54 c LoadBlock ; Load the next block with TurboLoad; with a stage wanted, check its byte at StageCheckByte; Z when right
> DI; Im2Jump := SavedLoaderBytes (the loader's code); TurboLoad; SaveLoaderBytes; SetIm2 (Im2Handler). StageLoaded 0 (the front): Z. Else Z when the byte at StageCheckByte equals StageCheck's for StageLoaded, NZ for another stage's block. A load error does not return here: TurboExit's RST 8 ends in the ROM's error report. Witness: L1 7 (c1, joystick, menu, stageload, rzx-r0, rzx-r1).

$FF7E b StageCheckFront ; Unused slot 0 of StageCheck (the front is not checked)
$FF7F b StageCheck 5 ; The byte at StageCheckByte of stages 1-5: $16, $4B, $FA, $E0, $80
> Read by LoadBlock (c1: stage 1; sN-right: stages 2-5). Each value is the stage block's byte at $BB80 (work/mkgame/stageN.bin).

@module font ; The print font and the glyph leftover

$FF84 b RomFontLeftover ; A copy of the ROM font $3E34-$3EAF (the end of F to U) and $27: no code reads it
> A leftover of the mastering: no operand names $FF84-$FFFF and the tape's image holds the ROM's bytes. The stack (SP = $FFFF) writes over its end in play. Known only from the code.
@res resident/rom-font-leftover.bin
